mathdb-lean problems
====================

This repository publishes benchmark releases of mathematical problems formalized
in Lean 4, together with the pinned Lean project they compile against.

VENDORED LIBRARIES
------------------

This repository root is itself the pinned Lean project, and carries two Lean
libraries taken from Formal Conjectures
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures), which is licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  upstream FormalConjecturesUtil/         -> MathDBUtil/,     MathDBUtil.lean
  upstream FormalConjecturesForMathlib/   -> MathDBMathlib/,  MathDBMathlib.lean
  LICENSE                                 (unchanged)

CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM, as Apache 2.0 section 4(b) requires them to be stated:

1. The two libraries' *module* names were changed to the two shown above, and
   their `import` lines and `lakefile.toml` entries were rewritten to match.
   Every Lean *namespace* inside them is upstream's, including `Google`, which
   holds the `answer()` elaborator, `FormalConjectures.Metadata`, and one per
   linter. `MathDBUtil/` was not otherwise touched.

2. This project is pinned to Lean 4.34.1 and Mathlib
   d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612, ahead of upstream's Lean 4.33.1 /
   Mathlib v4.33.1 (`lean-toolchain` and `lake-manifest.json` are therefore this
   project's, not upstream's). Twelve files under `MathDBMathlib/` were edited
   on 2026-10-08 so that they build there; each edit carries a comment dated
   2026-10-08 where it was made. In summary: declarations that Mathlib now
   provides under the same name were removed (SetTheory/Cardinal/Arithmetic,
   Data/Sym/Sym2, Algebra/Polynomial/HasseDeriv, Data/Finset/Powerset,
   AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Regulator, Data/Nat/MaxPrimeFac); two imports
   were added and one removed; one renamed Mathlib declaration was followed;
   three proofs were repaired. No surviving statement, definition or docstring
   was changed.

The upstream revision is recorded in each problem's `problem.toml` as
`[source] revision`, and in `benchmark.json`.

PROBLEM STATEMENTS
------------------

The problem modules under `problems/` come from two sources, and every module
and `problem.toml` records which, with the upstream file, declaration and
revision it came from. They are generated by the mathdb-lean problem library,
which is maintained separately; this repository holds its output.

* Formal Conjectures: derived mechanically from the vendored revision's
  `FormalConjectures/`, across twelve of its directories, which is likewise
  Apache-2.0.

* openai/math (https://github.com/openai/math, Copyright 2026 OpenAI, Apache
  License, Version 2.0): derived from the Lean challenge files
  `lean/ComparatorChallenges/*.lean` at revision
  fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM: each module
  reproduces the challenge's definitions, docstrings and statements verbatim
  under the `OAI` namespace, with two marked additions -- every `sorry`-bodied
  theorem is followed by a definition of the proposition it states, its section
  variables written out, and a `Problem.Target` conjoining those propositions is
  appended for the grader. The proofs upstream keeps in its `OAI` library are
  not copied. The accompanying catalogue under `openai-math/`
  (`MANUSCRIPTS.md`, `manuscripts.json`, `CATALOGUE.json`) is compiled from that
  repository's `CONTENTS.md`, `lean/docs/*.md`, `lean/formalization.yaml` and
  `history.md`: titles, descriptions, abstracts, scope notes and withdrawal
  notices, with a link to each manuscript's PDF in that repository at that
  revision. The manuscripts themselves are not redistributed. openai/math is a
  project of OpenAI; this repository is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  OpenAI.

MIRRORED STATEMENT CORPUS
-------------------------

`FormalConjectures/` is upstream's complete statement corpus at the same
revision, 1,416 `.lean` files and 4 `.md` files, mirrored so that the
`source_locator` each published obligation records resolves to a path inside
this repository rather than only inside a separate checkout.

CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM, as Apache 2.0 section 4(b) requires them to be stated:
on import lines only, the module `FormalConjecturesUtil` was renamed to
`MathDBUtil`, which is the same library under the name this project carries it
as (see VENDORED LIBRARIES above). That string occurs 1,418 times in the corpus
and all 1,418 are on an import line; 1,416 files carry one. Nothing else was
changed -- no declaration, statement, proof, docstring, attribute or internal
`import FormalConjectures.*` line. Files were written with LF endings; upstream
has no CR in this directory.

`FormalConjectures/MIRROR.json` records the upstream revision, the file count,
the single substitution and a digest over the whole tree, and `verify.py`
recomputes that digest, so a later edit to a mirrored statement is detectable.

These files are NOT part of the benchmark: none carries a `problem.toml`, a
target hash or any recorded evidence, and no admission profile admits them.
Most carry `sorry`, as upstream intends, since upstream is a statement
repository.

